            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0530" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/629a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan
                        (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-10T12:00:00-05:00">October 10,
                        1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. What significance do you attach to statement reportedly made yesterday by War
                    Office spokesman to Associated Press correspondent concerning possible Japanese
                    demand on Russia for “amends, retraction, and guarantee of future good faith.
                    Otherwise stronger measures may be necessary.”?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
